# =============================================================================
# variant-fm-benchmark — .gitignore
# Large / re-downloadable inputs, caches, scratch, and anything that could ever
# carry a credential are kept OUT of git. See README ("Data acquisition") for how
# to obtain every excluded input.
# =============================================================================

# --- Raw / intermediate data (large, re-downloadable) ------------------------
data/raw/
data/interim/
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bcf

# --- Reference genome & large binaries in refs/ (re-downloadable) ------------
# Keep the small provenance scripts (refs/*.sh, refs/*.py) and the GPN .tbi index;
# never commit FASTA/GTF/feature DBs (hundreds of MB to ~GB each).
refs/*.fa
refs/*.fa.gz
refs/*.fai
refs/*.fxi
refs/*.gtf
refs/*.gtf.gz
refs/*.gtf.db
refs/*.log

# --- Model-score caches & scratch (may be large; never the source of truth) --
# Belt-and-suspenders: cache files are excluded even outside data/raw/.
*cache*.json
*cache*.tsv
/score_matrix_final_with_nt.tsv
/nt_cache2.tsv

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Results scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
results/scratch/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
